 "verdict": "RECALL AT DEPTH, ON THE SUBSET THAT SUPPORTS IT. The request was recall@300 or @500; the first thing measured was whether those are answerable, and they are not in the sense intended. Across all 1400 knockouts the LARGEST specific-mover set is 246 genes, the median is 1, p99 is 210. NOT ONE knockout has 300 specific movers. So at K >= 300 every knockout's whole truth set fits inside the returned list and recall@K stops asking 'can you rank the right genes first' and starts asking 'are they anywhere in your top 300 of 7180'. THE SATURATION IS VISIBLE IN THE TABLES, not just argued: on the >=5-mover subset the DO-NOTHING TIDE BASELINE climbs from 0.250 at K=50 to 0.771 at K=500, so by K=500 a model that knows nothing about which gene was hit already recovers three-quarters of the truth. And MARKOV-P's STANDALONE contribution decays accordingly -- it closes 65% of the tide-to-oracle head-room at K=50 but only 3% at K=500. The K=300 and K=500 columns are therefore reported as SATURATION, not as success: raw recall there is high because the question got easier, not because the model got better. THE 'FULL DATA RANGE' SUBSET was defined rather than assumed: COMPLETE-CASE means every component genuinely has data for that knockout -- a codep partner in train for NEXUS, a physical neighbour for PHYS, a node in the protein chain -- so no component is credited on knockouts it silently declines to answer. Crossed with mover strata (>=5, >=20, >=50) it leaves progressively smaller test folds, and n is printed for every cell. THE PAIRED ENSEMBLE RESULT NEVERTHELESS SURVIVES AT EVERY DEPTH: on the >=50-mover complete-case subset the MARKOV-P gain over the 4-way ensemble is significant at K = [50, 100, 200, 300, 500], and its label-shuffled twin is negative at every one of them. But the gain SHRINKS with K exactly as the saturation predicts, and the honest summary is that the protein chain is a TOP-OF-LIST method: its value is in ranking the first few dozen genes, which is also the only regime a wet-lab follow-up could act on. Raw recall@K MUST rise with K and proves nothing alone, so three normalised views are reported next to it: lift over RANDOM (whose recall@K is exactly K/7180), the fraction of the tide-to-oracle head-room closed, and precision@K, which moves the opposite way and exposes list-padding. WHAT THIS CANNOT SAY: restricting to high-mover knockouts selects the strongest, most pleiotropic perturbations, which are not representative -- the median knockout has 1 specific mover and is invisible in these strata. Small folds at the top stratum mean absence of significance there is weak evidence, not evidence of absence. One cell line, 5 splits sharing the same underlying data. Deterministic given seed 0.",
 "note": "RECALL AT DEPTH, ON THE SUBSET THAT SUPPORTS IT. The request was recall@300 or @500; the first thing measured was whether those are answerable, and they are not in the sense intended. Across all 1400 knockouts the LARGEST specific-mover set is 246 genes, the median is 1, p99 is 210. NOT ONE knockout has 300 specific movers. So at K >= 300 every knockout's whole truth set fits inside the returned list and recall@K stops asking 'can you rank the right genes first' and starts asking 'are they anywhere in your top 300 of 7180'. THE SATURATION IS VISIBLE IN THE TABLES, not just argued: on the >=5-mover subset the DO-NOTHING TIDE BASELINE climbs from 0.250 at K=50 to 0.771 at K=500, so by K=500 a model that knows nothing about which gene was hit already recovers three-quarters of the truth. And MARKOV-P's STANDALONE contribution decays accordingly -- it closes 65% of the tide-to-oracle head-room at K=50 but only 3% at K=500. The K=300 and K=500 columns are therefore reported as SATURATION, not as success: raw recall there is high because the question got easier, not because the model got better. THE 'FULL DATA RANGE' SUBSET was defined rather than assumed: COMPLETE-CASE means every component genuinely has data for that knockout -- a codep partner in train for NEXUS, a physical neighbour for PHYS, a node in the protein chain -- so no component is credited on knockouts it silently declines to answer. Crossed with mover strata (>=5, >=20, >=50) it leaves progressively smaller test folds, and n is printed for every cell. THE PAIRED ENSEMBLE RESULT NEVERTHELESS SURVIVES AT EVERY DEPTH: on the >=50-mover complete-case subset the MARKOV-P gain over the 4-way ensemble is significant at K = [50, 100, 200, 300, 500], and its label-shuffled twin is negative at every one of them. But the gain SHRINKS with K exactly as the saturation predicts, and the honest summary is that the protein chain is a TOP-OF-LIST method: its value is in ranking the first few dozen genes, which is also the only regime a wet-lab follow-up could act on. Raw recall@K MUST rise with K and proves nothing alone, so three normalised views are reported next to it: lift over RANDOM (whose recall@K is exactly K/7180), the fraction of the tide-to-oracle head-room closed, and precision@K, which moves the opposite way and exposes list-padding. WHAT THIS CANNOT SAY: restricting to high-mover knockouts selects the strongest, most pleiotropic perturbations, which are not representative -- the median knockout has 1 specific mover and is invisible in these strata. Small folds at the top stratum mean absence of significance there is weak evidence, not evidence of absence. One cell line, 5 splits sharing the same underlying data. Deterministic given seed 0."
